module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ProjectiveSerreVanishing
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveCohomology.ModelComparison
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityIII.BlowupFibreDimension
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# A vanishing degree for the blowup read off a generating family of the ideal

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring and `I = (x₀, …, xₙ) ⊆ A`. The generating family presents the Rees
algebra as a graded quotient of `A[T₀, …, Tₙ]`, so the blowup `X` of `Spec(A)` in `I` is a closed
subscheme of `𝐏ⁿ_A` (`Stacks.Blowup.isClosedImmersion_blowUpSpecToProjSpace`). The cohomology of a
quasi-coherent module on `𝐏ⁿ_A` vanishes above degree `n` ([Stacks, Tag 01XI],
`Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.isZero_Hgroup_proj_of_lt`), and a closed immersion is affine, so
([Stacks, Tag 089W]) the same holds on `X` for every coherent module:

`Hⁱ(X, ℱ) = 0` for `i > n`.

The point of the bound is that it depends on the generating family alone. If `A → C` is any ring
map with `C` Noetherian, the images of `x₀, …, xₙ` generate `IC`, so the blowups of `Spec(C)` in
`IC` for all such `C` share the vanishing degree `n` — which is what Stacks 0GAR needs of the
invariant `d` of [Stacks, Tag 0GA6] for the perturbed quotients `P/(g'₁, …, g'_m)`, where the
source uses that `d` only depends on `Gr_I`. The witnesses
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.blowupDualSituationOfBound` accept any such degree.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.subsingleton_blowupHmod_of_span`: the vanishing.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 089W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/089W)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A)

/-- **`Hⁱ(X, ℱ) = 0` for a coherent `ℱ` on the blowup and `i > n`, when `I` is generated by
`n + 1` elements.** The blowup is a closed subscheme of `𝐏ⁿ_A`, where quasi-coherent cohomology
vanishes above degree `n`; see the module docstring. -/
@[ega "III 3.2.3" "special case"]
theorem subsingleton_blowupHmod_of_span {n : ℕ} (x : Fin (n + 1) → A) (hx : ∀ j, x j ∈ I)
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) (F : (blowupScheme I).Modules) [F.IsCoherent]
    {i : ℕ} (hi : n < i) : Subsingleton (blowupHmod I i F) := by
  set f := Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan
  have : ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).IsCoherent :=
    isCoherent_pushforward_of_isClosedImmersion f F
  have : ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).IsQuasicoherent :=
    isQuasicoherent_of_isCoherent _
  have : F.IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_of_isCoherent F
  refine subsingleton_blowupHmod I i F (AddCommGrpCat.subsingleton_of_isZero ?_)
  exact Stacks.Blowup.isZero_Hgroup_of_isZero_Hgroup_pushforward f F inferInstance i
    (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.isZero_Hgroup_proj_of_lt (R := A) n _ i hi)

end Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII

end
